1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,060
.

2
00:00:34,660 --> 00:00:35,490
Alice!

3
00:00:37,940 --> 00:00:38,960
Good morning!

4
00:00:40,520 --> 00:00:41,350
Busouka!

5
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:45,420
Good morning.

6
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:47,300
What brings you here?

7
00:00:47,680 --> 00:00:49,180
The weather's so nice.

8
00:00:49,420 --> 00:00:52,217
I thought we could take a
walk to the eastern hill.

9
00:00:52,300 --> 00:00:54,500
You, me, and Kirito, of course.

10
00:01:01,120 --> 00:01:02,857
It is a lovely day.

11
00:01:02,940 --> 00:01:04,822
The fresh air would do him good.

12
00:01:08,140 --> 00:01:10,160
Shall we go then, Kirito?

13
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:52,940
and

14
00:02:22,040 --> 00:02:25,517
I hope I'm feeling very happy?

15
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:26,717
I believe that I can't understand!

16
00:02:26,800 --> 00:02:31,097
I can't stand up to the
end of the whole time.

17
00:02:31,180 --> 00:02:33,140
This has been a great time!.

18
00:02:34,200 --> 00:02:36,494
I believed that I trusted a strong way.

19
00:03:04,460 --> 00:03:05,860
I believe?.

20
00:03:33,740 --> 00:03:35,257
Be careful with them.

21
00:03:35,340 --> 00:03:36,620
Hold them tight now.

22
00:03:43,260 --> 00:03:45,080
I hope he is warm enough.

23
00:03:47,040 --> 00:03:49,340
Sometimes you can be such a worrywart.

24
00:03:49,640 --> 00:03:52,052
You bundled him up so much he's sweating.

25
00:03:52,620 --> 00:03:53,940
Aren't you, Kirito?

26
00:03:58,920 --> 00:04:00,860
I know you, Gio, think so.

27
00:04:18,140 --> 00:04:19,460
How beautiful.

28
00:04:20,080 --> 00:04:24,340
None of the paintings in the
cathedral can compare with this view.

29
00:04:25,160 --> 00:04:28,160
You saved this world, Kirito. Remember?

30
00:04:30,620 --> 00:04:32,397
We're screwed! What do we do?

31
00:04:32,480 --> 00:04:36,460
If they cut the main power line
now, it's going to cause a surge.

32
00:04:37,060 --> 00:04:38,977
A light cube cluster should be safe,

33
00:04:39,060 --> 00:04:42,520
but the subcomputer where
Kirigai's STL is won't be.

34
00:04:42,760 --> 00:04:44,760
The surge will cook as Fluctlight.

35
00:04:46,080 --> 00:04:48,080
Okay, I'll handle the lockdown.

36
00:04:48,560 --> 00:04:49,600
Higa, take Dr.

37
00:04:49,760 --> 00:04:52,177
Kojiro and Asuna and
get to the upper shaft.

38
00:04:52,260 --> 00:04:54,660
Keep Kirito safe. Asuna?

39
00:04:55,300 --> 00:04:56,130
Kirito?

40
00:04:56,213 --> 00:04:57,277
They're cutting the power!

41
00:04:57,360 --> 00:04:59,478
The screw propellers are going down!

42
00:05:12,960 --> 00:05:13,790
Kirito!

43
00:05:15,740 --> 00:05:16,570
Kirito!

44
00:05:17,480 --> 00:05:18,310
Kirito!

45
00:05:18,720 --> 00:05:20,280
You cannot die!

46
00:05:20,460 --> 00:05:23,120
Not after saving my life! Kirito!

47
00:05:26,960 --> 00:05:27,790
Kirito!

48
00:05:30,140 --> 00:05:31,200
Hey, kid.

49
00:05:33,760 --> 00:05:34,590
Uncle…

50
00:05:34,673 --> 00:05:35,860
What happened?

51
00:05:38,440 --> 00:05:42,381
We're facing the biggest crisis in
the history of the Axiom Church.

52
00:05:42,680 --> 00:05:46,980
Those two elite disciples we
fought killed the Pontifex. No!

53
00:05:47,240 --> 00:05:48,140
It can't be!

54
00:05:49,080 --> 00:05:50,680
She's dead? Impossible!

55
00:05:52,220 --> 00:05:53,277
That's not all.

56
00:05:53,360 --> 00:05:55,242
Judelkin died with the Pontifex.

57
00:05:55,380 --> 00:05:57,615
With him gone, there's no more Senate.

58
00:05:58,860 --> 00:06:00,400
This makes no sense.

59
00:06:00,900 --> 00:06:04,257
Why would those disciples risk
angering the gods with their actions?

60
00:06:04,340 --> 00:06:08,997
To stop the Pontifex before she turned
half the human realm into weapons of war.

61
00:06:09,080 --> 00:06:11,300
An army of mindless, living swords.

62
00:06:11,840 --> 00:06:13,605
How could she do such a thing?

63
00:06:13,980 --> 00:06:16,320
To subject the people to such horror?

64
00:06:17,300 --> 00:06:18,420
It's diabolical.

65
00:06:19,040 --> 00:06:22,940
Ser Bercoli, where are the two
rogues who murdered her eminence?

66
00:06:23,220 --> 00:06:25,514
They must be captured and interrogated.

67
00:06:25,800 --> 00:06:28,257
We don't have time to
deal with that right now.

68
00:06:28,340 --> 00:06:31,105
The Dark Territory's been
itching to invade us,

69
00:06:31,220 --> 00:06:34,217
and when they find out about
the Pontifex, they will.

70
00:06:34,300 --> 00:06:38,617
Our ranks are half as strong thanks to
past battles with the forces of darkness.

71
00:06:38,700 --> 00:06:40,737
We should all be worried about that.

72
00:06:40,820 --> 00:06:46,540
If the Dark Territory decides to attack us
now, the human realm will fall for sure.

73
00:06:46,820 --> 00:06:48,173
Then what should we do?

74
00:06:48,260 --> 00:06:50,200
Or rather, what can we do?

75
00:06:50,360 --> 00:06:53,097
First, we'll restore the Order
of the Integrity Knights.

76
00:06:53,180 --> 00:06:55,777
Then we'll muster the Imperial Knights of

77
00:06:55,860 --> 00:06:58,389
the Four Empires and
train them for battle.

78
00:06:58,560 --> 00:07:03,031
There's strength in numbers, and right
now, we need all the help we can get.

79
00:07:03,200 --> 00:07:05,680
I know what I told you was hard to accept,

80
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:08,497
but it's still our job to
protect the people here.

81
00:07:08,580 --> 00:07:10,260
I can't do that without you.

82
00:07:11,520 --> 00:07:12,350
Sir.

83
00:07:37,620 --> 00:07:39,620
I wonder if Kirito's hungry.

84
00:07:40,600 --> 00:07:45,460
There's a rumor going round, saying that
rebel swordsman is still alive. I heard.

85
00:07:45,720 --> 00:07:47,485
He's supposed to be in a coma.

86
00:07:47,660 --> 00:07:50,877
I know we have to prepare for
the Dark Territory to invade,

87
00:07:50,960 --> 00:07:53,797
but leaving that traitor in our midst he

88
00:07:53,880 --> 00:07:56,377
defied the church and
should be executed for it

89
00:07:56,460 --> 00:07:59,157
agreed who knows what commander Bacoli is

90
00:07:59,240 --> 00:08:04,400
thinking it is no longer
safe for Kirito here?

91
00:08:23,360 --> 00:08:25,340
We shall go to Rulet Village.

92
00:08:25,880 --> 00:08:27,980
Perhaps they will accept us there,

93
00:08:28,260 --> 00:08:31,201
since it is the place where
Eugeo and I were born.

94
00:08:48,080 --> 00:08:49,160
Hold on, you!

95
00:08:49,540 --> 00:08:52,360
Strangers aren't allowed
in unless I say so!

96
00:08:59,300 --> 00:09:01,260
What in the...

97
00:09:01,820 --> 00:09:04,820
By the gods, it can't be.

98
00:09:05,040 --> 00:09:06,197
I am no stranger.

99
00:09:06,280 --> 00:09:07,520
I am Alice.

100
00:09:07,980 --> 00:09:09,860
Summon Gasfut Zuberg at once.

101
00:09:27,620 --> 00:09:30,700
Is that really you, Alice?

102
00:09:32,800 --> 00:09:33,630
Yes.

103
00:09:33,980 --> 00:09:36,420
Well then, what are you doing here?

104
00:09:36,660 --> 00:09:39,417
Have you been pardoned
for your crime? Perhaps.

105
00:09:39,500 --> 00:09:41,500
I certainly was punished for it.

106
00:09:41,940 --> 00:09:45,352
All of the memories I had of
my life here were wiped away.

107
00:09:45,580 --> 00:09:49,340
If that is not enough to absolve
me, no one said otherwise.

108
00:09:50,040 --> 00:09:51,980
Regardless, I have returned.

109
00:09:52,360 --> 00:09:54,948
Because I could think
of nowhere else to go.

110
00:09:59,400 --> 00:10:00,460
Be gone.

111
00:10:00,920 --> 00:10:03,680
We cannot allow a criminal to stay here.

112
00:10:13,900 --> 00:10:14,840
What's wrong?

113
00:10:19,320 --> 00:10:20,520
It is nothing.

114
00:10:21,400 --> 00:10:23,047
Shall we start heading back?

115
00:10:24,100 --> 00:10:24,940
Sure.

116
00:10:39,960 --> 00:10:41,540
What is it, Selka?

117
00:10:42,240 --> 00:10:43,820
Something troubles you.

118
00:10:45,600 --> 00:10:49,680
Well, it's nothing
serious. It's Mr. Barbosa.

119
00:10:50,320 --> 00:10:53,177
He asked if you could chop
down another tree for him.

120
00:10:53,260 --> 00:10:55,436
Honestly, that's why you're so quiet?

121
00:10:55,820 --> 00:10:58,173
You two know he and I have an agreement.

122
00:10:58,680 --> 00:11:00,500
Yes, but how dare he?

123
00:11:00,740 --> 00:11:01,780
The hypocrite!

124
00:11:01,980 --> 00:11:03,660
Both him and Mr. Riddick.

125
00:11:03,780 --> 00:11:06,597
They don't hesitate to ask you
for help when they need it,

126
00:11:06,680 --> 00:11:09,798
but they don't mind you
being shunned by the village.

127
00:11:13,660 --> 00:11:15,180
It's all right, Selka.

128
00:11:15,540 --> 00:11:19,599
As long as I can have a place on
the outskirts, that's enough for me.

129
00:11:20,160 --> 00:11:24,320
Yes, but next year, my training
will be done, and I was thinking,

130
00:11:24,680 --> 00:11:27,677
since I'll be earning a little
money, I could give you that.

131
00:11:27,760 --> 00:11:32,466
It's not much, but it's enough that you
won't have to help those people anymore.

132
00:11:33,120 --> 00:11:36,500
You and Kirito don't have to
worry. I'll help. Somehow.

133
00:11:39,920 --> 00:11:43,917
I'm grateful, but having you
close by is all I could ever need.

134
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:45,960
I'm happy just to have that.

135
00:11:46,800 --> 00:11:47,630
Sugou.

136
00:12:00,020 --> 00:12:01,820
Why is this taking so long?

137
00:12:02,040 --> 00:12:04,957
In the time it takes you
to cut this damn tree down,

138
00:12:05,040 --> 00:12:07,917
Riddick's men will have expanded
his land 20 miles in all directions.

139
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:08,830
Good day, Mr.

140
00:12:08,913 --> 00:12:09,743
Barbossa.

141
00:12:10,440 --> 00:12:11,270
Alice!

142
00:12:11,720 --> 00:12:13,240
How good of you to come!

143
00:12:13,360 --> 00:12:14,740
And so quickly, too!

144
00:12:15,180 --> 00:12:17,004
I heard you need my assistance.

145
00:12:18,260 --> 00:12:19,090
Yes.

146
00:12:19,173 --> 00:12:20,280
It's that one over there.

147
00:12:20,720 --> 00:12:23,597
We've been hacking away at
it since yesterday morning.

148
00:12:23,680 --> 00:12:26,060
These damn platinum oak trees are tough.

149
00:12:26,600 --> 00:12:27,430
Why,

150
00:12:27,513 --> 00:12:28,957
ten grown men have put
their backs into every

151
00:12:29,040 --> 00:12:31,017
swing and they've barely
made a scratch in it.

152
00:12:31,100 --> 00:12:32,460
So I asked for you.

153
00:12:32,720 --> 00:12:35,037
I know our deal is for one tree a month,

154
00:12:35,120 --> 00:12:38,617
but this one's stubborn and I
really need your help here, Alice.

155
00:12:38,700 --> 00:12:39,700
What do you say?

156
00:12:41,760 --> 00:12:43,840
I shall do it. And happily.

157
00:12:44,340 --> 00:12:46,240
But just this once, understood?

158
00:12:47,300 --> 00:12:48,130
Great!

159
00:12:48,213 --> 00:12:49,520
I knew I could count on you!

160
00:13:10,640 --> 00:13:15,160
If you don't mind, Kirito, I need
your sword, but only for a moment.

161
00:13:30,080 --> 00:13:30,940
Thank you.

162
00:13:37,220 --> 00:13:38,100
Come on.

163
00:13:38,320 --> 00:13:41,617
You think you're going to cut down a
platinum oak with a little old sword?

164
00:13:41,700 --> 00:13:42,820
It'll snap in half.

165
00:13:57,200 --> 00:13:58,360
Look at that.

166
00:13:58,500 --> 00:13:59,460
She missed!

167
00:14:02,400 --> 00:14:05,140
You'd best move away from there. What?

168
00:14:05,560 --> 00:14:06,880
Why should we...

169
00:14:30,540 --> 00:14:32,780
Oh. Splendid. Wonderful. Magnificent.

170
00:14:33,120 --> 00:14:34,980
Your skill is unbelievable.

171
00:14:35,440 --> 00:14:36,540
No, exceptional.

172
00:14:37,120 --> 00:14:38,320
Hear me out now.

173
00:14:38,580 --> 00:14:40,521
I shall double your compensation.

174
00:14:40,620 --> 00:14:43,637
And instead of once a month,
you'd work for me once a week.

175
00:14:43,720 --> 00:14:45,060
No once a day.

176
00:14:45,320 --> 00:14:46,877
I know you could use the money.

177
00:14:46,960 --> 00:14:50,725
Thank you, but the amount you are
paying now is quite sufficient

178
00:14:56,320 --> 00:15:01,020
My payment oh of course yes right away

179
00:15:04,640 --> 00:15:05,740
Thank you, mr.

180
00:15:05,860 --> 00:15:06,690
Barbosa

181
00:15:14,400 --> 00:15:15,230
What the?

182
00:15:15,313 --> 00:15:16,280
It's so heavy.

183
00:15:16,660 --> 00:15:18,877
How else do you think
she cut that tree down?

184
00:15:18,960 --> 00:15:20,557
Anyone could with that sword.

185
00:15:20,640 --> 00:15:21,470
Let me try.

186
00:15:31,920 --> 00:15:34,080
That sword belongs to Kirito.

187
00:15:34,540 --> 00:15:35,834
Get your hands off it.

188
00:15:37,180 --> 00:15:38,360
We asked him.

189
00:15:38,560 --> 00:15:42,325
If he didn't want us touching it,
he should have said something.

190
00:15:42,700 --> 00:15:43,530
He's right.

191
00:15:43,720 --> 00:15:48,600
We asked him nicely, and all he did
was go, uh, uh, like a gibbering fool.

192
00:15:54,620 --> 00:15:55,680
Fine, take it.

193
00:15:55,940 --> 00:15:57,460
It's just a damn sword.

194
00:16:20,260 --> 00:16:26,840
Is this what we fought for, suffered
for, to protect people like these?

195
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:30,740
Eugeo lost his life.

196
00:16:31,820 --> 00:16:34,280
Kirito is a shell of his former self.

197
00:16:34,920 --> 00:16:38,940
If there is a point to all we've
been through, it is lost to me.

198
00:17:03,080 --> 00:17:05,668
Amayori, it seems you've
gained some weight.

199
00:17:05,840 --> 00:17:08,100
You've been gorging on too many fish.

200
00:17:16,460 --> 00:17:18,640
Good night. Sleep well.

201
00:17:34,980 --> 00:17:35,840
Here.

202
00:17:43,720 --> 00:17:45,073
Don't eat too fast now.

203
00:17:58,720 --> 00:18:00,320
Is that...?

204
00:18:08,960 --> 00:18:09,790
Takiguri.

205
00:18:10,060 --> 00:18:11,437
I'm Ayori's elder brother.

206
00:18:11,520 --> 00:18:14,000
Which means...

207
00:18:17,400 --> 00:18:19,520
I'm impressed you found us.

208
00:18:19,740 --> 00:18:21,034
Now why have you come?

209
00:18:22,040 --> 00:18:23,720
Eldrie Synthesis 31.

210
00:18:25,020 --> 00:18:27,100
It has been far too long.

211
00:18:27,660 --> 00:18:29,880
My lady. My mentor.

212
00:18:33,520 --> 00:18:35,300
So how did you find me?

213
00:18:35,580 --> 00:18:37,460
More importantly, why?

214
00:18:38,140 --> 00:18:40,837
I'm sure the Order has
better things to do now

215
00:18:40,920 --> 00:18:43,802
than send dragons all over
just to track me down.

216
00:18:44,360 --> 00:18:49,160
You won't believe this, but I simply
followed the bond between our souls. Ha!

217
00:18:49,560 --> 00:18:50,913
If only that were true.

218
00:18:51,260 --> 00:18:53,613
No, I found you by complete coincidence.

219
00:18:53,880 --> 00:18:57,060
Although, now that I am here, I have news.

220
00:18:57,440 --> 00:19:00,675
The goblins and orcs have
been mobilizing in the north.

221
00:19:00,980 --> 00:19:02,480
As for why I'm here,

222
00:19:02,680 --> 00:19:06,977
the commander ordered us to collapse
the caves to the south and west and

223
00:19:07,060 --> 00:19:11,600
here in the north i was sent to make
sure the fiends hadn't dug them out

224
00:19:12,100 --> 00:19:16,897
and is the cave north of here safe
or have they dug through it i spent

225
00:19:16,980 --> 00:19:21,997
all day up there keeping a vigilant
eye upon it in all that time i did not

226
00:19:22,080 --> 00:19:27,077
spot any orcs or goblins i'm happy to
report the cave is still filled with

227
00:19:27,160 --> 00:19:33,400
debris then as i made my way back to
the capital takiguri began behaving

228
00:19:34,320 --> 00:19:35,150
strangely.

229
00:19:35,233 --> 00:19:38,637
I allowed him free rein, and
this is where he chose to land.

230
00:19:38,720 --> 00:19:40,540
Your new home, and

231
00:19:41,660 --> 00:19:46,237
now that we've been reunited at last,
you will forgive me for speaking my mind.

232
00:19:46,320 --> 00:19:48,960
Lady Alice, please return to the Order.

233
00:19:49,400 --> 00:19:52,460
We need your sword now,
more than ever, more than an

234
00:19:57,560 --> 00:19:58,390
army of thousands!

235
00:19:58,473 --> 00:20:00,037
I cannot. Why not?

236
00:20:00,120 --> 00:20:01,900
Is it because of that one?

237
00:20:02,180 --> 00:20:04,180
The man who escaped from prison?

238
00:20:04,360 --> 00:20:06,140
The man who flouted the law?

239
00:20:06,360 --> 00:20:09,237
Who raised his sword
against your fellow knights,

240
00:20:09,320 --> 00:20:11,438
the prime senator, and the pontifex?

241
00:20:11,600 --> 00:20:13,180
Is he still leading your

242
00:20:13,740 --> 00:20:14,570
heart astray?

243
00:20:14,653 --> 00:20:17,520
If so, there is but one
solution for your confusion.

244
00:20:18,140 --> 00:20:20,500
I shall eliminate him at once!

245
00:20:20,740 --> 00:20:21,640
Stop it!

246
00:20:22,820 --> 00:20:26,620
He fought not for himself, but
for what he believed was right.

247
00:20:27,100 --> 00:20:28,180
For justice.

248
00:20:28,520 --> 00:20:30,957
Is that not what the
knighthood fights for?

249
00:20:31,040 --> 00:20:33,057
He defeated us one after the other.

250
00:20:33,140 --> 00:20:34,552
including the commander.

251
00:20:35,160 --> 00:20:39,017
When you fought him, surely you could
feel the purity of his conviction?

252
00:20:39,100 --> 00:20:40,457
and the weight of his sword.

253
00:20:40,540 --> 00:20:45,305
If he is as pure as you say, then why
won't he take up his sword and help us now?

254
00:20:45,640 --> 00:20:49,717
How could he allow himself to be
reduced to such a pathetic state?

255
00:20:49,800 --> 00:20:51,976
and shackle you to these hinterlands?

256
00:20:52,140 --> 00:20:53,557
If what I heard is true!

257
00:20:53,640 --> 00:20:56,297
And he killed the Pontifex
for the sake of the people,

258
00:20:56,380 --> 00:20:59,217
Then it is his duty to join
them at the Eastern Gate.

259
00:20:59,300 --> 00:21:00,540
and defend the land!

260
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:05,737
Forgive me, Eldrie.

261
00:21:05,820 --> 00:21:08,717
But I cannot go with you
to assist in the battle.

262
00:21:08,800 --> 00:21:10,860
It has nothing to do with him.

263
00:21:11,360 --> 00:21:13,580
I can no longer wield my sword.

264
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:15,460
That is the reason.

265
00:21:15,820 --> 00:21:20,520
If you and I cross swords now, I
doubt I would last three strikes.

266
00:21:21,320 --> 00:21:22,500
Is that so?

267
00:21:22,960 --> 00:21:25,460
All right, I will not press you further.

268
00:21:33,200 --> 00:21:35,100
I bid you farewell, m 'lady.

269
00:21:35,400 --> 00:21:36,800
You were my mentor,

270
00:21:37,060 --> 00:21:41,040
and as long as I live, I shall
never forget all you have taught me.

271
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:42,882
Farewell, then.

272
00:21:43,420 --> 00:21:44,980
I pray you'll be safe.

273
00:22:10,880 --> 00:22:11,940
It's gotten late.

274
00:22:12,140 --> 00:22:13,197
You must be tired.

275
00:22:13,280 --> 00:22:15,104
Let's get you to bed, shall we?

276
00:22:40,600 --> 00:22:42,217
Tell me, Kirito.

277
00:22:42,300 --> 00:22:43,480
What should I do?

278
00:22:46,260 --> 00:22:47,860
What should I do?

279
00:23:04,020 --> 00:23:06,560
What is it? What's wrong?

280
00:23:25,560 --> 00:23:26,880
A fire!

281
00:23:27,160 --> 00:23:29,220
The Dark Territory is attacking!

282
00:23:31,720 --> 00:23:32,600
Sugou!

283
00:23:36,560 --> 00:23:38,060
Next time, the attack.
